cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or experimental data, please cite it as below."
title: "Spine Space Mesh: In-Flight Delay-Line Quantum Memory and Self-Healing Attractors on IBM Heron"
authors:
  - family-names: "Máté"
    given-names: "Róbert"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-3986-6039"
date-released: 2026-11-09
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/silentnoisehun/spine-space-mesh"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - "quantum-computing"
  - "ibm-quantum"
  - "delay-line-memory"
  - "superconducting-qubits"
  - "gross-pitaevskii"
  - "kuramoto-model"
  - "heron-r2"
  - "qiskit"
abstract: >-
  Implementation and physical quantum hardware validation of in-flight delay-line
  memory and continuous-time non-linear Gross-Pitaevskii attractors. Evaluated on the
  156-qubit IBM Heron processor (ibm_marrakesh), demonstrating 93.38% (1-cycle) and
  87.87% (2-cycle) X-basis state survival, with 50.30% classical mixture under severed-loop
  negative control.
